      "desc:8": "One entangler is a curio; a row of them is a mint. On plain steam at 80,000 L/s each singularity costs about 400,000,000 L of steam and 5,000 seconds of patience; superheated steam cuts the clock to 1,250 seconds at 320,000 L/s.\n\nThe crossover thresholds are 8 / 16 / 32 singularities on hand — enough to bind nodes, buy chips and still feed the DSM later. Show a stack of 32 to the quest book.\n\nRemember the saturation curve: past 200,000 L per cycle, extra steam buys less and less heat.",
